WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.152 --> 00:00:04.933
"Is your air on?"

2
00:00:05.353 --> 00:00:05.913
asks Josh.

3
00:00:05.933 --> 00:00:08.054
"Is your air on?"

4
00:00:08.414 --> 00:00:08.874
asks Anne.

5
00:00:08.894 --> 00:00:11.035
"Okay, let's go!"

6
00:00:12.355 --> 00:00:18.137
Today Josh and Anne are taking us on a scuba-diving adventure near the Similan Islands in Thailand.

7
00:00:18.977 --> 00:00:23.738
The water here is so clear that we can see things thirty meters away, and that's pretty far

8
00:00:23.798 --> 00:00:24.699
for being underwater!

9
00:00:26.379 --> 00:00:31.297
Whenever people go scuba diving, they swim in a group for safety, so we had better stay together!

10
00:00:31.977 --> 00:00:35.798
There are hundreds of great places to scuba dive in the world, and each of them is different.

11
00:00:36.739 --> 00:00:42.001
Some places are very cold, or are filled with seaweed, or have only very small animals.

12
00:00:43.281 --> 00:00:49.604
The Similan Islands, however, are great because the water is 28 degrees Celsius and crystal clear, and there

13
00:00:49.644 --> 00:00:50.684
are lots of big fish.

14
00:00:51.545 --> 00:00:52.705
In fact, look over there!

15
00:00:53.385 --> 00:00:55.886
Josh has found a moray eel hiding in the rocks.

16
00:00:56.707 --> 00:00:59.408
Don't worry; it is more frightened of us than we are of it.

17
00:01:01.588 --> 00:01:02.549
Look at its sharp teeth!

18
00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:07.431
It has two sets of jaws to pull its prey in, so keep your hands far away!

19
00:01:08.271 --> 00:01:12.273
Eels aren't very friendly creatures, as you can tell, and they mostly live alone.

20
00:01:12.893 --> 00:01:15.594
So we probably won't see another eel for quite a while.

21
00:01:16.835 --> 00:01:19.696
Did you know that there are hundreds of plants that live underwater?

22
00:01:20.356 --> 00:01:21.657
Thailand has many kinds.

23
00:01:22.597 --> 00:01:28.220
One plantlike creature is called coral, and there are two kinds: hard coral and soft coral.

24
00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:33.423
A coral is built from live cells that stack on top of each other in layers.

25
00:01:34.163 --> 00:01:38.826
When the outer layer gets old, a new layer of cells forms around it so the plant grows

26
00:01:38.886 --> 00:01:39.846
taller or wider.

27
00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:47.010
Like their names suggest, hard coral is stiff, while soft coral is able to sway with the ocean

28
00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:50.432
current. Both soft and hard coral grow very slowly.

29
00:01:51.292 --> 00:01:56.455
Look, this fan coral grows about one centimeter each year, so Anne is careful not to touch it

30
00:01:56.615 --> 00:01:57.476
as she swims by.

31
00:01:58.272 --> 00:02:03.054
Touching a coral can kill it, and sometimes it can hurt us too so we stay far away.

32
00:02:05.495 --> 00:02:09.497
Look, down at the bottom—there's a whale shark, the biggest fish in the world!

33
00:02:10.377 --> 00:02:14.859
Anne is trying to get her picture taken with it, but don't worry, this shark won't bite.

34
00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:20.542
Whale sharks only eat small animals and tiny plants that float in the water called plankton.

35
00:02:21.742 --> 00:02:25.544
Still, we're careful not to disturb the shark since this is its home.

36
00:02:26.548 --> 00:02:30.670
Josh is checking his pressure gauges, and signals to Anne that he is almost out of air.

37
00:02:31.731 --> 00:02:36.373
Men use up air faster than women because their lungs are bigger and because they have more muscle,

38
00:02:36.794 --> 00:02:39.995
but I think we have enough time to look at just a couple more creatures.

39
00:02:41.776 --> 00:02:43.897
Oh no, Anne is giving the danger signal!

40
00:02:44.678 --> 00:02:45.698
She found a sea snake.

41
00:02:46.279 --> 00:02:52.102
This underwater creature may be tiny, but its venom is twenty times more poisonous than any snake on

42
00:02:52.142 --> 00:02:57.460
land! It eats mostly small fish by paralyzing them first with one quick bite.

43
00:02:58.301 --> 00:03:00.441
It takes less than a second for its venom to work.

44
00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:04.202
The sea snake seems to be a little hungry, so we'll move on.

45
00:03:04.942 --> 00:03:07.363
Here is Josh's favorite animal, the cuttlefish.

46
00:03:08.163 --> 00:03:13.104
Many people eat cuttlefish thinking it is an ordinary squid, but it is really an amazing animal.

47
00:03:13.945 --> 00:03:14.605
Watch carefully.

48
00:03:15.225 --> 00:03:18.446
The mother cuttlefish is trying to protect its baby by distracting us.

49
00:03:19.386 --> 00:03:22.467
See how its skin is changing colors so that we can see it better?

50
00:03:23.367 --> 00:03:27.665
Cuttlefish can change the color and texture of their skin to match anything around them.

51
00:03:28.305 --> 00:03:33.648
For example, if there is a field of black rocks nearby, their skin will turn bumpy and black.

52
00:03:34.429 --> 00:03:38.091
If they swim by green seaweed, they will turn smooth and green.

53
00:03:38.952 --> 00:03:42.594
If you put down a purple polka-dot blanket, their skin will have polka dots!

54
00:03:44.315 --> 00:03:45.856
It looks like Josh is low on air.

55
00:03:46.756 --> 00:03:50.499
It's time to return to our own world above-water, but don't be disappointed.

56
00:03:51.119 --> 00:03:52.720
There will always be another adventure!
